From: Gemini CLI <gemini-cli@google.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 16:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] serial: 8250: silence rockchip-specific error prints

Permanently remove redundant pr_err calls in serial8250_handle_irq
that trigger on every frame error. This prevents console spam and
performance degradation on RK3566 when UART clock sync issues occur.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Rockchip-specific workaround]
Signed-off-by: Gemini CLI <gemini-cli@google.com>

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c
index 47d601e0e657..f765eb0c6470 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c
@@ -2012,18 +2012,7 @@ int serial8250_handle_irq(struct uart_port *port, unsigned int iir)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP
 	if (status & UART_LSR_BRK_ERROR_BITS) {
-
-		if (status & UART_LSR_OE)
-			pr_err("%s: Overrun error!\n", port->name);
-		if (status & UART_LSR_PE)
-			pr_err("%s: Parity error!\n", port->name);
-		if (status & UART_LSR_FE)
-			pr_err("%s: Frame error!\n", port->name);
-		if (status & UART_LSR_BI)
-			pr_err("%s: Break interrupt!\n", port->name);
-
-		pr_err("%s: maybe rx pin is low or baudrate is not correct!\n",
-			port->name);
+		/* Silence excessive Rockchip UART error logging */
 	}
 #endif
 	uart_unlock_and_check_sysrq_irqrestore(port, flags);
